#AI declaration
We used Claude (Anthropic) as a support tool during this delivereable.

**What we asked about:**
- Suggestions for how to solve the tasks, and explanations of the code
  line by line when needed
- Which parts of the code were covered in the lectures, and how to write
  type hints, docstrings and comments according to the course
- Debugging: a regex error in task 1 (`\.+?` instead of `.+?`), an indentation
  error in task 4, and a missing `data` folder
- Help with Git when we had problems committing and pushing
- What the output tables show, and how to interpret the results

**How AI contributed:**
- Claude suggested the first versions of the functions in tasks 3, 4 and 5,
  which we then modified, tested and integrated with our own code from tasks 1 and 2
- It helped us find and fix errors, and explained why they happened
- It suggested drafts for the discussion texts and the video script, which we
  rewrote and adjusted to our own results

**Our own work:**
We tested all code ourselves on our generated data, made our own choices
(for example function names, the handling of missing status columns, and the
JSON format for hourly revenue), and made sure we understand and can explain
all of the code.
